00:00:27.902 --> 00:00:28.737
Yeah.

00:00:28.737 --> 00:00:29.779
It's the gun.

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:30.739
-The gun is different.
-The gun.

00:00:30.739 --> 00:00:31.614
-The gun is...
-Yeah.

00:00:31.614 --> 00:00:32.323
Same eyebrows.

00:00:36.995 --> 00:00:38.913
I grew up not a huge gamer,

00:00:38.913 --> 00:00:40.874
but playing a lot of, uh like

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.667
kiddie games. My mom and I would play

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.711
Atari and stuff like that together.

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.337
So, when anybody in the neighborhood

00:00:46.337 --> 00:00:48.214
got a PlayStation it was a big deal.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.257
Hahahaha! 

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.015
Did you just explode Anthony?

00:00:57.015 --> 00:00:58.224
-Yeah.
-Anthony's dead.

00:00:58.808 --> 00:01:01.519
Our apocalypse happened in 2002.

00:01:01.519 --> 00:01:02.937
I wanted to do that because

00:01:02.937 --> 00:01:05.398
the 90s and 2000s was like when 
these games came out

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:07.525
and that's just so synonymous, 

00:01:07.525 --> 00:01:08.985
for me at least, with the time.

00:01:08.985 --> 00:01:09.569
Hahahaha!

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.571
You almost got us killed for a 
bunch of stupid CDs?

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.031
Stupid CDs?

00:01:13.031 --> 00:01:15.575
Good music is worth its 
weight in gold nowadays.

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:19.871
I got my first car around 2002

00:01:19.871 --> 00:01:23.291
and I loved playing my CDs and driving.

00:01:23.291 --> 00:01:27.629
So, I have a few scenes where 
I'm on the highway, jamming out,

00:01:27.629 --> 00:01:28.546
that's my favorite thing.

00:01:28.546 --> 00:01:29.506
What about you, Stephanie?

00:01:29.506 --> 00:01:31.841
I didn't learn to drive in high school.

00:01:31.841 --> 00:01:33.718
I just didn't learn,

00:01:33.718 --> 00:01:36.262
but I did ride passenger

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.472
-with all of my friends.
-Funny.

00:01:37.472 --> 00:01:39.724
The seat that I have in this show

00:01:39.724 --> 00:01:40.975
was what I was doing.

00:01:40.975 --> 00:01:43.478
I was helping navigate,
I was along for the ride.

00:01:43.478 --> 00:01:46.022
It'd be great if you could warn me before you drift like that.

00:01:46.022 --> 00:01:48.191
I f***ing slammed my g*****n 
head into the window.

00:01:48.191 --> 00:01:49.776
I said, "Hang on."

00:01:50.151 --> 00:01:51.903
Was there a stunt thing 
that you were like

00:01:51.903 --> 00:01:53.071
really wanted to do and 
were excited to do?

00:01:53.071 --> 00:01:54.030
Yeah, that fight!

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.115
That fight that I got to do.

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:55.698
That fight was awesome.

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:58.076
Because I like just stood there and
watched everything and I was like,

00:01:58.076 --> 00:02:00.787
"I think I could do that you know, you should let me try that."

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.664
By the end, I had done the whole thing

00:02:02.664 --> 00:02:03.915
which was exciting.

00:02:03.915 --> 00:02:04.666
That was cool.

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:06.918
You know what I didn't enjoy,

00:02:06.918 --> 00:02:08.920
learning how to drive stick in 15 minutes
-Oh right!

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:12.340
so that Anthony could run into the car
while I was driving it.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:13.383
The whole time I was just like,

00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:15.176
"It's Anthony Mackie! It's 
Anthony Mackie!"

00:02:15.176 --> 00:02:17.053
"Don't kill Anthony Mackie!" You know?

00:02:18.054 --> 00:02:19.722
-But I think it was okay.
-It worked!

00:02:19.722 --> 00:02:21.558
-It worked perfectly.
-It worked great!

00:02:21.558 --> 00:02:22.267
Hang on.

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:23.184
Thanks for the warning.

00:02:25.228 --> 00:02:27.981
The most fun was driving
through the mall.

00:02:28.606 --> 00:02:31.442
So if I'm here, then the exit is...

00:02:31.442 --> 00:02:32.777
Oh, they have a Foot Locker!

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:35.530
And they're like, "Oh well you know

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:37.740
we wanna grab these shoes and 
do this and do that

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:39.534
and you know just don't hit the wall."

00:02:39.784 --> 00:02:42.328
I'm like, "I'm not gonna hit
the wall, I can drive."

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:45.874
So I can literally say I
drove through a mall

00:02:45.874 --> 00:02:48.418
and scooped some shoes off the rack.

00:02:50.253 --> 00:02:53.464
I think the great thing about
John is he's so...

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:56.634
angelic in the way he looks at life.

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:59.596
He's such a simple guy.

00:02:59.596 --> 00:03:01.514
He thinks he has it all figured out

00:03:01.973 --> 00:03:06.102
and with that comes a certain
naivety that he has

00:03:06.102 --> 00:03:10.148
that really gives a spark to his
character that you never really see

00:03:10.565 --> 00:03:14.944
and kinda takes the frustration
out of something like an apocalypse.

00:03:14.944 --> 00:03:16.029
What I love too about like

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:17.906
I remember our early
conversations about John--

00:03:17.906 --> 00:03:19.824
-Oh!
-Oh!

00:03:19.824 --> 00:03:21.075
-Ah, double death.
-Nope!

00:03:21.075 --> 00:03:21.659
Was that...

00:03:21.659 --> 00:03:23.161
I think we're both...no you killed me!

00:03:23.161 --> 00:03:24.162
-I think you died under me!
-You killed me!

00:03:24.162 --> 00:03:25.038
Haha!

00:03:25.788 --> 00:03:26.456
That was cool!

00:03:26.664 --> 00:03:27.624
You wanna do multiplayer again?

00:03:27.624 --> 00:03:29.334
-No no no, I'm going one player, you talk.
-Oh, you’re going one player.

